7. Create Models
ada = AdaBoostClassifier(random_state=42)gbm = GradientBoostingClassifier(random_state=42)xgb = XGBClassifier(    random_state=42,    eval_metric="mlogloss")



Here, we create three different ensemble learning models.

A. AdaBoost
ada = AdaBoostClassifier(random_state=42)



- Creates an AdaBoost classification model.
- AdaBoost stands for Adaptive Boosting.
- It gives more importance to incorrectly classified data points in subsequent training.
B. Gradient Boosting
gbm = GradientBoostingClassifier(random_state=42)



- Creates a Gradient Boosting model.
- It builds models sequentially.
- Each new model tries to reduce the errors made by the previous models.
C. XGBoost
xgb = XGBClassifier(    random_state=42,    eval_metric="mlogloss")



- Creates an XGBoost classification model.
- XGBoost stands for Extreme Gradient Boosting.
- It is an optimized and efficient implementation of gradient boosting.
- random_state=42: Makes results reproducible.
- eval_metric="mlogloss": Uses multiclass log loss as an evaluation metric during training.
